  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1101.01 Purpose",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1101.01 Purpose. The purpose of the rules in Env-Wq 1100 is to:\n\n(a) Establish the criteria and procedures for reviewing and approving the design and installation of public bathing places;\n\n(b) Identify standards to protect water quality and the health and safety of persons using public bathing places;\n\n(c) Ensure that public bathing places are maintained and operated safely for patrons; and\n\n(d) Implement:\n\n(1) RSA 485-A:26, II(b) relative to registration of PBF establishments;\n\n(2) RSA 485-A:26-a relative to PBF compliance self-certification;\n\n(3) RSA 485-A:27, II relative to emergency closures;\n\n(4) RSA 485-A:27-a relative to certified pool operators; and\n\n(5) RSA 485-A:26, IV relative to equivalent municipal programs.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100) #8468, eff 11-1-05; ss by #10577, eff 5-1-14 (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100); ss by #13198, eff 5-1-21 (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1100.html"
